WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:07.819
The Commonwealth of Fallout 4 is full of desolate
wonder and interesting characters—​who

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:09.490
you can then kill and loot.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:13.169
It's also home to some locations that wouldn't
be out of place in Freddy Krueger's ambien-fueled

00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:14.169
nightmares.

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:18.020
It doesn't matter how decked out your Power
Armor is, because fear can penetrate the hardiest

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.080
of suits.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.259
Grab your security blanket, duck under the
covers, and check under the bed for feral

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:26.640
ghouls as we dive into these pulse-raising
locations.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.640
Swan's Pond

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.990
While it's not very scary on the surface,
Swan's Pond near Boston Common is terrifying

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.440
for another reason.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.860
You might think you're just passing by a pond,
with nothing noteworthy around, but then it

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.030
happens: the ground begins to rumble.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.440
You turn around just in time to see the ugly
face of one of the game's Unique Super Mutant

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.440
Behemoths named Swan who, incidentally, has
a big plastic swan strapped to his shoulder.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.700
If you don't become a crater within the first
few seconds of encountering him, you might

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.810
just be able to take him down to get a legendary
furious power fist weapon.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.830
That is, if you don't crap your pants when
you first encounter him.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.100
Suffolk County Charter School

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.330
A school in the middle of a post-apocalyptic
wasteland?

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.049
How creepy could it be?

00:01:05.049 --> 00:01:08.480
Of course, the answer is "very, very creepy,
indeed."

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.610
What makes Suffolk County Charter School unique
is the school's history.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.680
If you look into the background of the school,
you'll find out how it was a part of a government

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.150
experiment called the Nutritional Alternative
Paste Program.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.490
That means that the school swapped out its
rubbery chicken nuggets and crappy pizza for

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:22.490
pink sludge.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.670
So, in other words, it was an upgrade.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:28.380
Still, apparently the paste increased aggression
in the students and actually turned their

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.380
skin a little pink.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.840
While that's pretty gross, fans of Fallout
are no strangers to seeing the results of

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.380
experiments gone awry.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.000
But there's something more unnerving than
usual to walk into the school and see all

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.930
the feral ghouls with bubblegum-pink skin.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:41.930
Dunwich Borers

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:46.400
Ah, the Dunwich Borers, a place where hope
goes to die and where your sense of reality

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.900
goes to get warped.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.610
If you're at all familiar with the works of
H.P.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:53.210
Lovecraft, then you might have picked up on
the reference to "The Dunwich Horror," a short

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.350
story written in 1928.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.900
You might also recognize the name "Dunwich"
because it appeared in Fallout 3 in the form

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.310
of the Dunwich Building, a dungeon that featured
a lot of supernatural phenomena and was arguably

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.630
the creepiest place in the the Capital Wasteland.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:09.700
The Dunwich Borers is a dig site that looks
innocent enough...or as innocent as a place

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.349
in a Fallout game can get.

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:13.160
But it hides a terrible secret.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.909
As you get clamber deeper into the pit, you'll
witness supernatural flashbacks akin to the

00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:21.049
ones from the Dunwich Building and a bunch
of feral ghouls trying to gnaw your face off.

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:24.849
If you venture deeper, you can find a dagger
called Kremvh's Tooth at the bottom of a well.

00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:29.140
You'll also see part of a face poking out
of the water, presumably belonging to a statue

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.969
of some elder god or some kind of entity worshipped
by the Dunwich company.

00:02:33.969 --> 00:02:35.799
Milton Parking Garage

00:02:35.799 --> 00:02:37.529
Remember the Saw movies?

00:02:37.529 --> 00:02:40.590
Remember how badly you wanted to feel like
you trapped in one of them, but only lacked

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.639
the psychotic friends necessary to make your
dreams come true?

00:02:43.639 --> 00:02:47.730
Well good news: ​Fallout 4​'s Milton Parking
Garage has got you covered.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.749
Located next to the Milton General Hospital,
the labyrinthine, booby-trapped garage, contains

00:02:51.749 --> 00:02:55.669
devices designed to maim you, locked-room
puzzles, and even more mannequins, placed

00:02:55.669 --> 00:02:58.760
there with the sole purpose of giving players
the heebie-jeebies.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.599
Creepier than the dungeon itself is the question
that looms after you've escaped: who put this

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.459
whole, crazy thing together and why?

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:07.629
And seriously, where's he getting all the
mannequins?

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:11.150
It looks like a J.C. Penney on coupon day.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.719
Museum of Witchcraft

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:17.450
One of the absolute coolest places in all
of the Commonwealth is The Museum of Witchcraft.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:21.150
And it's one you should probably avoid if
you're not armed to the teeth.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.700
You'll actually be sent here if you pick up
the quest called "The Devil's Due" and decide

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.590
to track down some missing soldiers that belong
to the Gunners, but it's still best to wait

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.090
until you're really ready to deal some damage.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.019
The front doors are locked tight, so you'll
need to enter the building through the basement.

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:37.920
If you have Stealth Boys, you'll want to use
them, because you'll immediately discover

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.950
that you're not alone in the building.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.079
Floorboards creak and inhuman noises fill
the air.

00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:46.999
Experienced players will recognize the sound
as everyone's favorite monster: a Deathclaw.

00:03:46.999 --> 00:03:50.620
And not only does that Deathclaw stalk you
through the museum's halls, but around every

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.349
corner you'll encounter a bunch of spooky
mannequins meant only to raise your blood

00:03:54.349 --> 00:03:55.840
pressure even more.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.389
If you manage to avoid or kill the beast,
you can loot a mound of Deathclaw eggs.

00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:01.790
And you know what that means: omelettes for
everyone!

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:06.029
Or, more accurately, a whole lot of caps.

00:04:06.029 --> 00:04:07.089
Pickman Gallery

00:04:07.089 --> 00:04:09.862
This place will really make you wonder whether
or not you should help everyone you meet in

00:04:09.862 --> 00:04:11.169
the Commonwealth.

00:04:11.169 --> 00:04:14.510
Upon entering the Pickman Gallery, you'll
see a bunch of disturbing paintings hanging

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.630
on the wall, all painted with vibrant reds
and yellows.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.590
Heh, kinda like Nintendo Pikmin.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.340
They all show scenes pulled straight out of
depths of hell.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.780
Or maybe just a typical day at Five Guys Burgers
and Fries.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.330
We're not quite sure.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.990
More to the point, you'll see a bunch of raiders
trying to kill a man named Pickman.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.070
Should you choose to save him, he'll drop
some creepy lines of gratitude and give you

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:36.740
a key that lets you loot a safe for a weapon
called Pickman's Blade.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.340
Once you really take a look around and see
all of the buckets of blood and dismembered

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.889
body parts everywhere, and then think about
the name of the weapon, it'll dawn on you

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:46.729
that Pickman is a maniac who paints those
freakish paintings using the blood of his

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:47.729
victims.

00:04:47.729 --> 00:04:50.349
So that answers that question: those are definitely
pictures of Five Guys.

00:04:50.349 --> 00:04:52.740
Or, you know, ground up Nintendo Pikmin.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.740
Either way.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:54.740
Thanks for watching!

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.610
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.860
And leave us a comment to tell us which Fallout
4 location put you off solid food for the

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:00.870
longest.

